credits='''<div class="wrap"><article class="legal-page"><p class="eyebrow">Acknowledgements</p><h1>Illustration &amp; type.</h1><h2>Original illustrations</h2><p>The editorial artwork was generated for this blog using contrasting media: collage, painted still life, glass and metal sculpture, and geometric print art. These are illustrations of ideas, not photographs or records of Ahmad’s personal experiences. Personal and London photographs were supplied by Ahmad. Their original appearance is preserved; web copies are resized and compressed. The guest badge QR code was removed for display. KFUPM photographs are credited below.</p><h2>Photographs</h2><p>The personal and London collection was supplied by Ahmad. The photographs are presented without AI reconstruction or color filters; the guest badge QR code was removed. WebP copies retain their original proportions. The KFUPM campus photograph and portrait of Laqman were supplied by Ahmad. These two photographs are preserved as supplied, displayed within decorative frames without AI reconstruction or color filters.</p><h2>Videos</h2><p>Embedded videos are by 3Blue1Brown and remain hosted on YouTube. Original vector studies are used on video cards; they are not frames from the videos. Homepage cards link directly to YouTube. Article players load only after consent and a Play action.</p><h2>Typography</h2><p>Source Serif 4 and DM Sans are freely available fonts, locally hosted under the SIL Open Font License. Font licences are included in the downloadable source package.</p><h2>Book covers</h2><p>Real edition covers identify the books discussed. Harry Potter covers are by Bloomsbury and were retrieved through Open Library and bookseller cover catalogues. Nicola Yoon covers were retrieved from Penguin Random House. The twenty additional covers identify established NYT bestselling titles and were retrieved from publishers and Open Library. Cover artwork belongs to the respective illustrators and publishers; source URLs and ISBNs are recorded in assets/book-covers/credits.json. Book summaries use original wording.</p><h2>The animated bookshelf</h2><p>The pixel-book animation adapts a reference supplied by Ahmad and appears only in the homepage reading section. Its yellow, green, and lilac palette matches the blog. Animation is optional, respects reduced-motion preferences, and makes no external requests.</p><h2>Brand icons</h2><p>The YouTube, LinkedIn, X and Instagram glyphs come from Bootstrap Icons under the MIT license. The license is included in assets/social/bootstrap-icons-LICENSE.txt.</p><h2>The miniature worlds</h2><p>The drawing studio, observatory and electronics workshop are original pixel artwork rendered locally. They include scene selection and pause controls, respect reduced motion, and stop when offscreen.</p><h2>Design &amp; writing</h2><p>The layout, styles, interactions, and editorial text were created for Ahmad Alabbas. The editorial direction draws inspiration from Gates Notes. No Gates Notes source code, photographs, logos, or proprietary fonts are included.</p></article></div>'''
